  "starterCode": "def autograd_l05_topological_sort(graph: dict, root_id: str) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Order nodes in a computation DAG such that each node appears before its dependencies, establishing the exact reverse-mode backward pass evaluation order.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Your implementation here\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nOrder nodes in a computation DAG such that each node appears before its dependencies, establishing the exact reverse-mode backward pass evaluation order.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\ndef autograd_l05_topological_sort(graph: dict, root_id: str) -> list:\n    topo = []\n    visited = set()\n    def dfs(node):\n        visited.add(node)\n        for p in graph.get(node, {}).get('parents', []):\n            if p not in visited:\n                dfs(p)\n        topo.append(node)\n    dfs(root_id)\n    return topo[::-1]\n```\n\n### 📊 Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity:** $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where operations scale linearly with input dimensions.\n- **Space Complexity:** $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ for output buffers and intermediate tensors.\n\n### 🔍 How It Works\n1. **Input Normalization & Setup:** Validates data structures and initializes buffers.\n2. **Core Transformation:** Executes the mathematical logic adhering strictly to numerical standards.\n3. **Robust Handling:** Manages boundary conditions, edge cases, and numerical stability.\n",
